# ///////////////////////////////////////////////
# Project
# ///////////////////////////////////////////////
#
# Everything this project ignores on its own account. The upstream block
# below is a swappable unit, so anything added here stays here through a
# refresh.

# Build output
dist/
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Coverage. The upstream block covers these too, under *.out, coverage.*
# and *.coverprofile. They are spelled out here because the coverage task
# and .testcoverage.yml name these exact files, so this section stays
# readable on its own.
coverage.out
coverage.txt
coverage.html
*.coverprofile

# The commitlint and Prettier install package.json names
node_modules/

# IDE. Upstream ships the first two commented out; the rest it omits.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local-only notes (not committed)
*.local.md
*.local.*

# Operator's own build settings, which Taskfile.yml loads, and the other env
# files Bun loads from the directory it starts in. Each belongs to one
# contributor, and the gate refuses a tracked one. .env.template is generated
# and committed.
.env
.env.local
.env.development
.env.development.local
.env.production
.env.production.local
.env.test
.env.test.local
!.env.template

# Per-machine Claude Code settings, beside the committed settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Code review artifacts (local only)
.claude/review/

# Worktrees the Claude Code CLI creates inside this repo
.claude/worktrees/

# lefthook's per-user overrides, which it merges over lefthook.yml, and their
# scripts. The gate refuses a tracked one.
lefthook-local.*
.lefthook-local.*
.lefthook-local/

# ///////////////////////////////////////////////
# Upstream: github/gitignore, Go.gitignore
# ///////////////////////////////////////////////
#
# From revision 1d7e3275a461, dated 2025-01-12, with one edit: coverage.* is
# anchored to the root, where the coverage task writes it, because the
# unanchored pattern also matches a source file named coverage.go in any
# package. Refresh by replacing everything below this header with the output
# of the command below, then carry that edit:
#
#   gh api repos/github/gitignore/contents/Go.gitignore --jq '.content' | base64 -d

# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts. Anchored to the root,
# where the coverage task writes them: an unanchored coverage.* also matches
# a source file named coverage.go in any package.
*.out
/coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
